  "setKeepAliveTitle": "Keep the mesh running in the background",
  "setKeepAliveBody": "Shows a notification while it runs, and uses some battery. Without it Android may stop Bluetooth work soon after you lock the phone, and some phones do so even with it. This has not been tested on real phones yet.",
  "setKeepAliveRefused": "Android did not allow it right now. Try again with the app on screen.",
  "setBackgroundUse": "Background use",
  "setBackgroundUseBody": "This phone suspends the app soon after you lock it or leave it, and nothing the app can ask for changes that. Messages are exchanged while the app is open.",
  "setBatteryTitle": "Battery restrictions",
  "setBatteryRestricted": "On: to save battery, Android may stop دەمەتەقێ in the background, even with the setting above. To keep the mesh running with the screen off, open the battery settings and choose \"Unrestricted\" (the words differ from phone to phone).",
  "setBatteryUnrestricted": "Off: Android lets دەمەتەقێ run in the background without battery restrictions. Some phone makers add restrictions of their own.",
  "setBatteryOpen": "Open battery settings",
  "setBatteryCouldNotOpen": "This phone did not open its battery settings. Look for دەمەتەقێ under Apps in the phone's settings.",
  "setPermBluetooth": "Bluetooth (nearby devices)",
  "setPermBluetoothWhy": "To find and talk to phones near you. Never your location.",
  "setAllowed": "Allowed",
  "commonAllow": "Allow",
  "setPermMic": "Microphone",
  "setPermMicShort": "Only while you record a voice message",
  "setPermCamera": "Camera",
  "setPermCameraShort": "Only to take a picture you want to send",
  "setPermPhotos": "Photos",
  "setPermPhotosShort": "Only to pick a picture you want to send",
  "setPermNotifShort": "Only to tell you a message arrived while the app is not on screen",
  "honestyNoInternetTitle": "No internet, no accounts, no servers",
  "honestyNoInternetBody": "Messages travel from phone to phone over Bluetooth Low Energy. Nothing is sent to the internet or to any company, and there is nothing to sign up for.",
  "honestyRangeTitle": "Range, relaying and waiting",
  "honestyRangeBody": "One Bluetooth link reaches roughly 10 to 30 metres, less through walls. If phones with the app are in between, a message can hop through them: up to {direct} hops for private messages and {group} for groups and public rooms. If nobody is in reach, a private message or a group message is kept and retried for up to {directHours} hours (public rooms: {roomHours} hours), then it is marked as not delivered. Phones that pass group and public traffic along also keep it for people who arrive later. Relaying has been tested with simulated radios only; it has not yet been proven on real phones, so use the Bluetooth self-test and your own phones to see how it behaves in practice.",
  "@honestyRangeBody": {
    "placeholders": {
      "direct": {
        "type": "int"
      },
      "group": {
        "type": "int"
      },
      "directHours": {
        "type": "int"
      },
      "roomHours": {
        "type": "int"
      }
    }
  },
  "honestyMediaTitle": "Pictures, voice messages and videos",
  "honestyMediaBody": "Pictures are shrunk to a few dozen kilobytes (about 640 pixels wide), voice messages are limited to {seconds} seconds, and videos are not shrunk at all: only a very short clip fits (you choose the limit under Settings > Storage). Bluetooth is slow: each hop takes a few seconds, more with several hops or a weak signal. Every file is checked against its SHA-256 before it is shown. In a group a picture or a video can stay incomplete if a piece of it is lost on every path; it then shows as not received. Videos cannot be sent to public rooms. Pictures, recordings and videos are kept in the app's private storage, not in your gallery, unless you choose \"Save to gallery\".",
  "@honestyMediaBody": {
    "placeholders": {
      "seconds": {
        "type": "int"
      }
    }
  },
  "honestyBackgroundTitle": "The background is not guaranteed",
  "honestyBackgroundBody": "دەمەتەقێ works best while it is open. Phones restrict what apps may do with Bluetooth in the background, and this app does not try to get around that. On Android you can switch on \"Keep the mesh running in the background\": it shows a notification while it runs and lets the app stay alive more often, but it is no guarantee, and it has not been tested on real phones yet. Phones that are locked or have the app closed may relay nothing.",
  "honestyPrivateTitle": "Private chats",
  "honestyPrivateBody": "Private messages, pictures and voice messages are end-to-end encrypted: only the person you send to can read them, even when other phones pass them along. Phones that pass something along can see who sent it and who it is for (their public keys), roughly when, and its approximate size, but not the content. Anyone nearby can see that a phone is advertising دەمەتەقێ, and the name you chose.",
  "honestyGroupsTitle": "Groups",
  "honestyGroupsBody": "A group is private: its messages are encrypted with a key that only its members have, and nothing about it (its name, its members, that it exists) is ever broadcast. Only the person who created it can add or remove people, and every change gives the group a new key, so someone who was removed cannot read what is sent afterwards. They keep what they already received. If a key change reaches a member later than the messages sent right after it, those messages may be missed.",
  "honestyRoomsTitle": "Public rooms",
  "honestyRoomsBody": "A public room is NOT private. Everything said in it - text, pictures and voice - can be read by every phone that carries it, and by anyone who joins. Messages are signed, so a relay cannot change a word or forge an author, but names can be chosen freely: the short id after a name is what tells two people with the same name apart. The built-in #mesh room is for everyone nearby; rooms people create are announced to nearby phones and disappear after a day unless their creator's phone keeps renewing them. Messages in public rooms are removed from this phone six hours after they arrive.",
  "honestyDeleteTitle": "Deleting and editing",
  "honestyDeleteBody": "Delete for me removes a message from this phone only. Delete for everyone sends a request to the other phones: it works only if they receive it in time, and it cannot reach a copy somebody saved or photographed. Editing sends the new text in the same way. Both are possible for two days after a message is sent.",
  "honestyVerifyTitle": "Who are you really talking to?",
  "honestyVerifyBody": "The first time two phones meet, there is no way to know a key is really that person's. Open their contact page, compare the safety number with them in person or on a call you trust, and only then mark them verified. Until then, treat names as unverified.",
  "honestyStoredTitle": "What is stored on this phone",
  "honestyStoredBody": "Your keys (and the keys of your groups) are kept in the phone's secure storage (Android Keystore / iOS Keychain). Chat history, pictures and recordings are stored in the app's private storage without an extra layer of encryption beyond your phone's own lock screen and disk encryption, and on an iPhone they may be included in device backups. Anyone who unlocks your phone can read your chats.",
  "honestyAuditTitle": "Not independently audited",
  "honestyAuditBody": "The encryption uses standard algorithms (HPKE with X25519 and ChaCha20-Poly1305, Ed25519 signatures), and the core encryption is tested against the published test vectors. But this app's code has not been reviewed by an independent security expert. Do not rely on it where your safety or freedom depends on it.",
